  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Modulo \\(5,\\) the equation gives \\(3x\\equiv1,\\) so \\(x\\equiv2\\pmod5.\\) Write \\(x=2+5k.\\) Then \\[ y=\\frac{501-3x}{5}=99-3k. \\] Positivity requires \\(k=0,1,\\ldots,32,\\) giving \\(33\\) pairs.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Reduce the equation modulo \\(5\\) to find the form of \\(x\\)",
        "Count the positive values \\(x=2+5k\\) that leave \\(y\\gt0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
